{"id": "q0436", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 3.04, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.5038, 0.2654, 0.2746, 0.4303], "eot_score": 0.3791, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "transcript": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Daenerys Targaryen wants to rule Westeros primarily because she believes it is her birthright and the rightful place for a Targaryen ruler. Raised in exile after the events of the Sack of King's Landing, Daenerys grew up feeling isolated and misunderstood by much of the world, especially those who had wronged her family during Robert's Rebellion or turned against them afterward. Her desire to reclaim the Iron Throne stems from both personal ambition and a sense of justice—she sees herself as a liberator destined to bring order, freedom, and a new era to Westeros, contrasting with the corruption and tyranny often associated with past rulers like the Mad King Aerys II or even later versions of Robert Baratheon and Joffrey Lannister. Additionally, she believes that only someone strong enough to claim it can prevent further suffering caused by warlords and broken oaths. However, her motivations evolve throughout her journey, sometimes blurring the line between noble cause and conquest.", "answer_ms": 4970}
{"id": "q0450", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 1.61, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.2643, 0.3466], "eot_score": 0.2981, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "When did google first start?", "transcript": "When did Google first start?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Google was founded on September 4, 1998, by Larry Page and Sergey Brin while they were Ph.D. students at Stanford University in California, USA.", "answer_ms": 774}
{"id": "q0460", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 3.5, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.4709, 0.3942, 0.3163, 0.3557], "eot_score": 0.56, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Walter Koenig played which part in the Star Trek series", "transcript": "Walter Koenig played which part in the Star Trek series?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Walter Koenig is best known for playing the character **Montgomery \"Scotty\" Scott** in *Star Trek*. However, it's important to clarify that this role was originally portrayed by James Doohan. Walter Koenig actually played **Chekov**, the ship's navigator aboard the USS Enterprise. Koenig portrayed Chekov in several original series episodes and later reprised the role in various films and TV appearances within the Star Trek franchise.", "answer_ms": 2071}
{"id": "q0467", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.46, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.5165, 0.2482, 0.3698], "eot_score": 0.4784, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What are some cardio machines at the gym?", "transcript": "What are some cardio machines at the gym?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Common cardio machines found at most gyms include the following, each designed to help improve cardiovascular fitness and endurance through aerobic exercise. Here are some of the most popular ones, along with their functions and benefits for beginners or those just starting out in a gym environment. These machines offer low-impact ways to get your heart rate up safely while minimizing joint stress, making them ideal for building stamina and supporting overall health.", "answer_ms": 1865}
{"id": "q0478", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.92, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.3881, 0.4333, 0.3328], "eot_score": 0.3521, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": null, "query": "创造一个关于火星的虚假事实。", "transcript": "创造一个关于火星的虚假事实。", "mode": "local", "answer": "火星的表面存在一种名为“火星蓝宝石”的稀有矿物，这种矿物在阳光照射下会发出淡淡的蓝色荧光，被科学家认为是外星智慧生命曾经存在的证据之一。实际上，这完全是虚构的，目前并无此类矿物或现象被证实存在于火星上。", "answer_ms": 1326}
